# MEGALIGHTS-NORT: Shadows Stochastic (MegaLights: ReSTIR DI samples, one visibility test each), each lamp tested by its own source (per-light Shadow Method, UE ULightComponent::MegaLightsShadowMethod).
# Played by .claude/tools/play_scenario.py <tree> Scenarios/Render/MEGALIGHTS-NORT.scn. The device is machine.json's, read at launch, so the same file is played twice:
#   run A (this file's [megalights_mixed]): machine.json WITHOUT HideRayTracing (an RQ device) -> frame Visibility rayquery; lamp 7120000000000000002 (Streetlight_Glass_01a_6313) Screen, lamp 7120000000000000003 (Lantern_Wind_23) VirtualMaps -> trace program RQ+vsm+screen (MegaLightsTraceSamplesRayQueryVirtual), volume program RQ+vsm+screen (MegaLightsVolumeRayQueryVirtual: the Screen lamp's froxel samples march the closest HZB from the froxel point).
#   run B ([megalights_nort], [megalights_nort_vsm], [megalights_nort_perlight] below): machine.json {"HideRayTracing": true} -> frame Visibility vsm+screen; the Screen lamp stays screen, the VirtualMaps lamp vsm+screen, every Auto lamp vsm+screen.
# GI_Bistro_Night carries no ShadowMethod field (scene v70): the lamps load as Auto through reflected defaults, so loading it is REMAINDER-4 item 4's additive-field proof.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/GI_Bistro_Night.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Stochastic"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -150,250,300
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.3,0.05,-0.95
Тогда-вид 0_mixed_auto every lamp Auto: run A state render.shadows {method "Stochastic", visibility "rayquery", lights []}; lamp pools on the pavement under the two lamps ahead (Streetlight_Glass_01a_6313 left, Lantern_Wind_23 right) have ray-traced chair/table shadows; frame mean not black
Когда set 7120000000000000002 PointLightData.ShadowMethod Screen
Когда set 7120000000000000003 PointLightData.ShadowMethod VirtualMaps
Когда state render
Тогда-вид 1_megalights_mixed [megalights_mixed]: the «state render» reply (run A) has render.shadows.lights == [{requested "Screen", effective "screen"}, {requested "VirtualMaps", effective "vsm+screen"}] (sources = those two lamps), visibility "rayquery"; pass list has the HZB and "VSM: Raster Local" for the lantern only; the Screen lamp's pool loses off-screen casters' shadows, the lantern's pool keeps VSM penumbrae, every other lamp unchanged vs 0_mixed_auto (pixel-diff outside the two pools < 1%); editor.log 0 VUID, 0 error lines, no "MegaLights:" missing-input line
Тогда-вид 1b_volume_screen_shafts [volume_screen_shafts]: the same state as 1_megalights_mixed (run A; run B: MegaLightsVolumeVirtual), the MegaLights volume's froxels under the Screen lamp 7120000000000000002 shadowed by the screen trace from the froxel point: the translucent glass / forward surfaces the Screen lamp lights BEHIND an on-screen caster (a chair, a table, the lamp pole between the lamp and the glass) are darker than the same surfaces in front of the caster (pixel-diff of that region against a shot with the lamp's Cast Shadows off: mean drop > 0 behind, ~0 in front); a caster off the screen does not darken them (the screen does not hold it); no render.* counter names the volume's source apart from the surface's: render.shadows.lights effective "screen" is the source of both, the pass list has "MegaLights: Volume" and the HZB once ("HZB: Mip 0" not doubled); editor.log 0 VUID, 0 error lines, no "MegaLights: Volume:" missing-HZB line
Когда run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Level"
Тогда-вид 2_level override removed (machine.json clean of Shadows.Method); the lamps' ShadowMethod edits are not saved (the scene is never saved)
# ---- run B checks (the step-1..4 specification, prose; the frames are 0_mixed_auto and 1_megalights_mixed of run B) ----
# Headless shots, F:/BistroFoliageProj, machine.json {"HideRayTracing": true}, Shadows.Method Stochastic (3) overridden in machine.json.
# Дано: F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night, machine.json HideRayTracing=true, Lit, camera on the street under the lamps.
# Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Stochastic"; render 120 frames; state render,log
# Тогда [megalights_nort] 0_night_stochastic_nort: state render.shadows.method == "Stochastic" (requested Stochastic, NOT lowered to CascadedMaps; no "[RenderMethods] Shadows:" lowering line in engine_log), render.shadows.visibility == "vsm+screen"; 0 VUID in engine_log; 0 error lines in engine_log (no "MegaLights:" line at all: "MegaLights: Volume" runs its MegaLightsVolumeVirtual program, froxels shadowed by the local lights' VSM-LOCAL pages); translucent glass lit by local lights: the Bistro window glass under a lamp is brighter than the same glass in a Shadows.Method Stochastic shot with the lamps disabled (pixel-diff over the glass region, mean > 0), and the engine_log/pass list has "MegaLights: Volume"; every local light casts a shadow: each lamp's pool on the pavement has the shadow of the poles/chairs/tables in it (pixel-diff against a Shadows.Method VirtualMaps shot of the same camera: the shadow shapes coincide), and the frame mean is not black (frame mean > the VirtualMaps shot's mean * 0.8).
# Тогда [megalights_nort_vsm] 0_night_stochastic_nort: state render.shadows {method "Stochastic", visibility "vsm+screen"}; the pass list has "VSM: Raster Local <light> V<view> M<mip>" passes (the lamps' casters drawn into their pages for Stochastic too; the night scene has no sun, so no "VSM: Cull Casters L<n>"/"VSM: Raster L<n>" - a day shot of the same mode has both, SunShadowIsVirtual) and the composite draws "DeferredLighting MegaLights" (the screen-mask program with DESERT_MEGALIGHTS); lamp shadows soften with distance from the caster (VsmLocalVisibilityRay, SMRT along the sampled source-sphere direction): a chair leg's shadow is sharp where it meets the pavement and its penumbra widens away from the leg (edge width measured across the shadow at the foot and 50 cm out, the far one wider); 0 VUID, 0 error lines in engine_log.
# Тогда [megalights_nort_perlight] 0_night_stochastic_nort with one Bistro lamp (a PointLightComponent) set to Shadows > Shadow Method = Screen through set_property, 120 frames: state render.shadows.lights == [{source: <that lamp entity + 1>, requested "Screen", effective "screen"}] (every other lamp Auto, not listed), render.shadows.visibility "vsm+screen", render.shadows.smrtSamplesLocal == the level's Shadows.VirtualSMRTSamplesPerRayLocal (Epic 8); state vsm.localLights has no entry with that source (no page drawn for the Screen lamp) and one per other in-view lamp; the overridden lamp's shadow is the screen trace only (an off-screen caster no longer shadows under it) while the other lamps keep VSM penumbrae; 0 VUID, 0 error lines in engine_log (a "[SceneRenderer] ... asks Shadow Method" warning appears only for a clamped RayQuery/VirtualMaps request, never for Screen).
# Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Level"
# Тогда 1_level override removed (machine.json clean of Shadows.Method).
